 "drivingQuestion": "What does the mishna's 'for vegetables' refer to?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "'For vegetables' is glossed as the vegetable tithe",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "rosh_hashanah.12a.6",
   "daf": "12a",
   "sentenceId": 5,
   "he": "וְלַיְּרָקוֹת. תָּנָא: לַיְּרָקוֹת וְלַמַּעַשְׂרוֹת וְלַנְּדָרִים. לַיְּרָקוֹת מַאי נִינְהוּ? מַעֲשֵׂר יָרָק.",
   "en": "§ The mishna taught: «And» the first of Tishrei is the new year «for vegetables.» It «is taught» in a baraita: The first of Tishrei is the new year «for vegetables, and for tithes, and for vows.» The Gemara asks: «What is» meant by the term: «For vegetables?» It means «for» the «vegetable tithe,» i.e., one may not take teruma or tithes from vegetables picked before Rosh HaShana in order to fulfill the obligation for vegetables picked after Rosh HaShana."
  }
 ],
